      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.24,
          "end": 3.073,
          "en": "Now sometimes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.073,
          "end": 5.06,
          "en": "you want more detailed insights.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.06,
          "end": 8.5,
          "en": "You don't just want to console lock something.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.5,
          "end": 10.23,
          "en": "When using React Native,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.23,
          "end": 12.3,
          "en": "especially also with Expo,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 12.3,
          "end": 14.52,
          "en": "you get some additional tools.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 14.52,
          "end": 18.34,
          "en": "Now for this let's press question mark here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 18.34,
          "end": 19.68,
          "en": "in our terminal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 19.68,
          "end": 21.68,
          "en": "where we started npm-start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 21.68,
          "end": 25.17,
          "en": "to see a full list of available shortcuts we can use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 25.17,
          "end": 28.37,
          "en": "whilst this npm-start process is running.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 28.37,
          "end": 31.61,
          "en": "So you just need to activate this terminal, this console",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 31.61,
          "end": 32.64,
          "en": "by clicking into it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 32.64,
          "end": 34.97,
          "en": "and then you can use the shortcuts you see here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 34.97,
          "end": 36.91,
          "en": "to trigger certain things.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 36.91,
          "end": 40.01,
          "en": "For example, we did press A, to open the app on Android",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 40.01,
          "end": 42.64,
          "en": "or I, to open it on iOS before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 42.64,
          "end": 45.82,
          "en": "You can for example, also press R, to force a reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 45.82,
          "end": 47.94,
          "en": "I also did that before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 47.94,
          "end": 49.81,
          "en": "Now, what's quite interesting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 49.81,
          "end": 52.07,
          "en": "is that you can also",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 52.07,
          "end": 55.5,
          "en": "press M, to toggle a menu,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 55.5,
          "end": 58.53,
          "en": "to be precise a developer menu.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 58.53,
          "end": 60.25,
          "en": "If you press M here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 60.25,
          "end": 64.38,
          "en": "this menu opens up on one of the two emulators",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 64.38,
          "end": 68.89,
          "en": "which you can also open by pressing Command-D on iOS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 68.89,
          "end": 72.37,
          "en": "or Command or Control-M on Android.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 72.37,
          "end": 74.5,
          "en": "Alternatively, press M here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 74.5,
          "end": 76.86,
          "en": "in the terminal to open it as you saw.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 76.86,
          "end": 79.02,
          "en": "And then in this developer menu,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 79.02,
          "end": 80.85,
          "en": "you can also force a reload.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 80.85,
          "end": 84.6,
          "en": "You can go back to the homepage of your app here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 84.6,
          "end": 87.56,
          "en": "but you can also do a couple of other things.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 87.56,
          "end": 90.813,
          "en": "For example, you can debug JavaScript remotely.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 91.72,
          "end": 93.24000000000001,
          "en": "If you click on this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 93.24000000000001,
          "end": 96.49000000000001,
          "en": "a new tab in Chrome should open up,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 96.49000000000001,
          "end": 97.86,
          "en": "and in that tab,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 97.86,
          "end": 101.16,
          "en": "you can open up the Chrome Developer Tools",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 101.16,
          "end": 103.72,
          "en": "and in those developer tools, you can, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 103.72,
          "end": 106.97999999999999,
          "en": "see network requests made by your app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 106.97999999999999,
          "end": 110.47999999999999,
          "en": "At the moment our app isn't making any network requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 110.47999999999999,
          "end": 113.72999999999999,
          "en": "but you could see network requests made by your app here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 113.72999999999999,
          "end": 116.52000000000001,
          "en": "if it's reaching out to some backend or anything like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 116.52000000000001,
          "end": 120.35,
          "en": "Here, we just see some development and debugging assets,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 120.35,
          "end": 122.15,
          "en": "which are downloaded. (alert chiming)",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 122.15,
          "end": 123.95,
          "en": "And you also see a console",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 123.95,
          "end": 126.71,
          "en": "where you can see the log messages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 126.71,
          "end": 129.31,
          "en": "your app might be generating.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 129.31,
          "end": 131.98,
          "en": "For example, if I go back to my code here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 131.98,
          "end": 135.293,
          "en": "and I re-add console.log \"GoalInput\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 136.44,
          "end": 139.28,
          "en": "here in the goal input component and I save this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 139.28,
          "end": 142.28,
          "en": "In that console, you should also see output generated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 142.28,
          "end": 144.68,
          "en": "by the running app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 144.68,
          "end": 146.01,
          "en": "If you don't see it here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 146.01,
          "end": 148.27,
          "en": "you might need to force a reload",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 148.27,
          "end": 150.71,
          "en": "or even restart the iOS app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 150.71,
          "end": 152.65,
          "en": "I did have problems with that before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 152.65,
          "end": 154.2,
          "en": "it can be a bit clunky",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 154.2,
          "end": 157.77,
          "en": "but ultimately you should see some output here as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 157.77,
          "end": 161.37,
          "en": "Now, this is just an additional way of looking into your app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 161.37,
          "end": 164.3,
          "en": "and especially having a look at the network requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 164.3,
          "end": 167.23,
          "en": "could be something that is interesting.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 167.23,
          "end": 170.2,
          "en": "Now you can at any time, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 170.2,
          "end": 172.04,
          "en": "stop remote debugging",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 172.04,
          "end": 176.45,
          "en": "to go back to the old state, like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 176.45,
          "end": 177.48,
          "en": "It's just an addition,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 177.48,
          "end": 179.5,
          "en": "not something you have to use all the time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 179.5,
          "end": 180.64,
          "en": "and probably not something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 180.64,
          "end": 182.983,
          "en": "you want to use all the time.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
